# Generated, team-specific content: repo lists, workspace context, model pins.
# It stays out of this public template by default. A private fork that tracks this
# repo as upstream may well want it committed -- that is the intended way to share a
# harness with a team. To do that, add `!config/` below this line (or delete the rule).
#
# The rule is path-agnostic, so it also swallowed examples/acme/config/ -- which is
# committed worked-example content, not generated state. Hence the negation.
config/
!examples/acme/config/

# Team instantiation: the answers file and the workspace context for a specific
# team. Untracked on purpose -- this repo is the generic core, and a real team's
# repo names, org, and product details must never land in it. The files stay on
# disk; move them between machines out of band (private gist, password manager,
# scp), not through this repository.
instantiation/

# Runtime state: logs, PID file, the usage journal.
var/

# Local secrets. Copy .envrc.template to .envrc; never commit the result.
.envrc

.venv
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
litellm.log
*.db

# Tool caches produced by linting the harness itself.
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
